course: dictionary
lesson: 10129
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word thread can mean a string for sewing, but it can also mean a line of ideas in a talk. «I lost the thread» does not mean you dropped a string. It means you lost track of what someone was saying.
explain: Read the words around the word. «She threaded the needle with blue thread» is about sewing, because the needle is the clue. «The thread of the story got tangled» points to ideas, not string, because a story has no string to tangle.
explain: Swap in your meaning and check. If "long, thin string" still makes sense in «most of it is a web of fine threads hidden in the soil», you have probably got it. If "a line of ideas" makes sense in «I lost the thread», that is your answer.
fact: Thread (noun) is a long, thin string of cotton, silk or nylon used for sewing.
fact: «I lost the thread» means you lost the line of ideas in a story or talk.
fact: To thread a needle means to push thread through its hole.
fact: «Hang by a thread» means to be in great danger.
fact: A thread online is a list of messages about one topic.
exercise: «Peel back the husk and each long silky thread leads to one kernel.» What is a thread in this sentence? | A tool for cutting corn | A line of ideas in a talk | A list of messages about one topic | *A long, thin strand
exercise: Mia says, «I lost the thread.» What does she mean? | She has found a spider's web | She has dropped a reel of sewing thread | She has tied a knot in her shoelace | *She has lost track of what was being said
exercise: «Please thread the beads onto the string.» What does thread mean here? | To tie a knot in the sewing | To hang by a thread | *To put the beads on a string | To cut the string into pieces
test: «The climber was hanging by a thread.» What does hang by a thread mean? | To be very long and thin | Hanging from a tall tree | *To be in great danger | Sewing with a needle
test: «A thread online is a list of messages about one topic.» Which meaning of thread is this? | A needle hole | A string of cotton | *A list of messages about one topic | A spiral ridge on a screw
exam: Ravi reads, «Most of the fungus is a web of fine threads hidden in the soil.» What does thread mean here? | To push through a needle's hole | *Long, thin strands | Messages on one topic | Lost track of what was said
